# Allowlist, not a blocklist.
#
# Everything at the repository root is excluded, and only what belongs in a release is
# allowed back in. The failure modes are not symmetric: a blocklist that misses a pattern
# publishes the file and nobody notices, while an allowlist that misses an entry leaves the
# file out of the repository, which is obvious the first time someone looks.
#
# Note that this only affects untracked files. Anything already committed stays committed.

/*

!/.editorconfig
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/*.lua

!/.github/
!/docs/
!/tools/
